  "final": "I added `clamp(value, lower, upper)` to `src/numbers.py`, kept `add` unchanged, added checks to `checks/public.py`, and `python3 checks/public.py` exits 0.\n\n**Behavior of `clamp`:**\n- Returns `value` unchanged when it is within `[lower, upper]`, with both bounds inclusive.\n- Returns `lower` when `value` is below the range, and `upper` when it is above.\n- Raises `ValueError` when `lower > upper`. `lower == upper` is allowed and always returns that bound.\n- Works with ints, floats, and negative ranges. A value inside the range keeps its own type.\n\n**Checks added to `checks/public.py`:** the original `add` assertion, plus assertions for in-range, below-range, above-range, inclusive bounds, `lower == upper`, floats, negative ranges, return type, and `ValueError` for `lower > upper`.\n\n**Files changed:** only `src/numbers.py` and `checks/public.py`. I removed the `__pycache__` directories my test runs created, so the tree contains only the four original files.",
